<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Dedicated guidance where none previously existed</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 3041 provides DEDICATED recognition and MEASUREMENT guidance FOR agricultural INVENTORIES and PRODUCTIVE biological ASSETS — a GENUINE gap PREVIOUSLY absent FROM ASPE, REQUIRING enterprises TO apply Section 3031 (INVENTORIES) or SECTION 3061 (PROPERTY, Plant and EQUIPMENT) by ANALOGY, DESPITE neither STANDARD being WELL-suited to the DISTINCTIVE characteristics OF biological growth AND agricultural production.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Two Categories</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Agricultural inventories and productive biological assets</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Category</span><span>Description</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Agricultural inventories</span><span>HARVESTED products OF biological ASSETS held FOR sale, PROCESSING, or CONSUMPTION (e.g. HARVESTED grain, RAISED livestock intended FOR sale)</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Productive biological assets</span><span>LIVING plants OR animals held FOR their PRODUCTIVE capacity OVER multiple PERIODS (e.g. DAIRY cattle, FRUIT-bearing trees), RATHER than FOR immediate SALE or CONSUMPTION</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Agricultural Inventories</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Harvested outputs, distinct from the biological assets that produced them</div><div class="text-supporting">AGRICULTURAL inventories are THE harvested, TANGIBLE outputs OF an enterprise'S biological ASSETS — GENUINELY distinct FROM the underlying PRODUCTIVE biological asset ITSELF. WHERE a SECONDARY production PROCESS transforms an AGRICULTURAL inventory into a FURTHER end-USE product (e.g. GRAPES into WINE), the RESULTING product IS generally accounted FOR as ORDINARY inventory under SECTION 3031, OUTSIDE this Section'S own scope.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Productive Biological Assets</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Held for ongoing productive capacity, not immediate sale</div><div class="text-supporting">PRODUCTIVE biological ASSETS are HELD for THEIR ongoing PRODUCTIVE capacity OVER multiple PERIODS — SUCH assets are AMORTIZED over THEIR useful LIFE, MUCH as an ORDINARY item of PROPERTY, plant, AND equipment WOULD be, GIVEN their SIMILARLY long-TERM, capacity-GENERATING role WITHIN the enterprise'S operations.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>THE MEASUREMENT CHOICE — Net Realizable Value or Cost</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A genuine accounting policy election</div><div class="text-supporting">ASPE PERMITS an ENTERPRISE to ELECT, AS an accounting POLICY choice, EITHER the NET REALIZABLE VALUE model (MEASURING agricultural INVENTORIES and PRODUCTIVE biological ASSETS at THEIR estimated SELLING price LESS costs TO sell, WITH changes RECOGNIZED in NET income) OR the COST model (HISTORICAL cost, LESS accumulated AMORTIZATION and IMPAIRMENT, FOR productive BIOLOGICAL assets; LOWER of cost AND net realizable VALUE, for AGRICULTURAL inventories) — a GENUINE choice, RATHER than a SINGLE mandated APPROACH.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Why This Genuinely Distinguishes ASPE From IAS 41</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A meaningful contrast with IAS 41's fair value default</div><div class="text-supporting">INTERNATIONALLY, IAS 41 GENERALLY requires FAIR value measurement FOR biological ASSETS as the DEFAULT approach (WITH cost only PERMITTED in NARROW circumstances WHERE fair VALUE cannot be RELIABLY measured). ASPE, BY contrast, GIVES private ENTERPRISES a GENUINE, unrestricted CHOICE between NRV and COST — a DELIBERATE simplification REFLECTING that MANY private AGRICULTURAL enterprises LACK ready ACCESS to RELIABLE, active-MARKET fair VALUE data, and that COST-based measurement is OFTEN more PRACTICAL and LESS costly to APPLY for SMALLER operations. INTERESTINGLY, THIS ALSO differs FROM Chinese GAAP'S ASBE No. 5 (see the COMPANION Chinese GAAP poster EARLIER in this LIBRARY), WHICH treats COST as the DEFAULT with FAIR value as a NARROW exception — ASPE'S own APPROACH sits GENUINELY in BETWEEN, offering BOTH as EQUALLY legitimate ALTERNATIVES.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Assets Outside This Section's Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Land and non-productive agricultural assets remain under other Sections</div><div class="text-supporting">FARMLAND ITSELF, and OTHER agricultural-related ASSETS not MEETING the DEFINITION of AGRICULTURAL inventory OR productive BIOLOGICAL asset, CONTINUE to be ACCOUNTED for UNDER their OWN respective GOVERNING Sections (e.g. SECTION 3061 for LAND).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Measuring Agricultural Inventory Under the NRV Model</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognizing changes in value directly in net income</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Harvested grain, electing the NRV model</div><div class="wk-body">A grain farming enterprise, electing the net realizable value model, harvests 50,000 bushels of wheat with an estimated selling price of $8.50 per bushel and estimated selling costs of $0.30 per bushel.</div><div class="wk-answer">The COMPANY measures the AGRICULTURAL inventory AT 50,000 × ($8.50 − $0.30) = <strong>$410,000</strong>, with ANY subsequent CHANGE in this NET realizable VALUE recognized DIRECTLY in NET income.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Amortizing a Productive Biological Asset Under the Cost Model</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Treating a productive biological asset much like PP&amp;E</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A dairy herd, electing the cost model</div><div class="wk-body">A dairy operation, electing the cost model, acquires productive dairy cattle for $600,000, with an estimated 8-year productive useful life.</div><div class="wk-answer">The COMPANY amortizes the CATTLE at $600,000 ÷ 8 = <strong>$75,000 per year</strong>, LESS than accumulated AMORTIZATION and any IMPAIRMENT, MUCH as it WOULD depreciate an ORDINARY item of PROPERTY, plant, AND equipment under SECTION 3061.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 3041 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Measurement model elected (net realizable value or cost) for agricultural inventories and productive biological assets</span><span>Carrying amounts of agricultural inventories and productive biological assets</span><span>Gains and losses recognized during the period under the elected model</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Classifying an asset as agricultural inventory versus a productive biological asset</span><span>Which measurement model (NRV or cost) best serves the enterprise's circumstances</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Net realizable value, where elected</span><span>Useful life of productive biological assets, underlying the amortization calculation</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 41</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASPE Section 3041 vs IAS 41</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 3041</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 41</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Default measurement basis</span><span>Genuine choice — NRV or cost</span><span>Fair value, with cost only in narrow exceptions</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY significant DIVERGENCE — ASPE'S own FLEXIBLE, choice-BASED approach STANDS in CONTRAST to IAS 41'S fair-VALUE-forward default, REFLECTING ASPE'S broader COST-conscious orientation TOWARD private ENTERPRISE reporting.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every agriculture-related event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>NRV model gain/loss</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Recognized directly in net income</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Cost model amortization</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Systematic expense over useful life, similar to PP&E</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 3031</span><span>Inventories — the general standard this Section carves agricultural inventories out from</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 3061</span><span>Property, Plant and Equipment — the general standard this Section's cost-model amortization mechanics parallel</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Productive biological asset</div><div class="glossary-def">A living plant or animal held for its ongoing productive capacity over multiple periods, rather than for immediate sale.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Agricultural inventory</div><div class="glossary-def">A harvested, tangible output of a biological asset, held for sale, processing, or consumption.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.aspe3041 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
